      "model_text": "Cursor is an integrated development environment (IDE) and software development platform designed to assist engineers with building, navigating, and debugging codebases. Available as a native desktop application across macOS, Windows, and Linux, it provides code editing, file navigation, and terminal execution. The platform also offers command-line tools (CLI), cloud agent environments, and integrations with source control systems such as GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket, and Azure DevOps.\nAI is central to Cursor's product architecture rather than an optional add-on. Documented AI capabilities include: - Agent and Composer: Autonomous workflows capable of searching repositories, planning changes, editing across multiple files, and executing shell commands from natural-language instructions. - Codebase Understanding & Chat: Semantic code indexing to answer questions, explain architectures, and assist with debugging. - Code Review & Automated Workflows: Features such as Bugbot for automated pull-request reviews, automated tracking of AI-generated commits, and cloud-hosted agent tasks. - Model Orchestration: Support for routing queries across frontier large language models (including Claude, Gemini, and Grok).",
