      "model_text": "GitHub Copilot is an AI-powered developer assistant designed to assist engineers throughout the software development lifecycle. It provides real-time code completions, generates multi-step implementation plans, answers natural language questions about codebases, and automates pull request reviews. Copilot operates natively across several surfaces, including integrated development environments (IDEs), command-line interfaces (CLI), dedicated desktop applications, and directly within GitHub.com.\nAI capabilities are central and foundational to GitHub Copilot, not an optional secondary feature. The product relies on underlying large language models to deliver its core capabilities, which GitHub documents across assistive and agentic categories: real-time code generation, interactive contextual chat, automated test generation, pull request explanation and review, and autonomous agent tasks (such as editing files, running tools via the Model Context Protocol [MCP], and submitting changes for developer review).",
